Subject: [PATCH] winedmo: use a zero-based byte position for codec parsers

av_parser_parse2's final argument is a byte position, not a timestamp.
AV_NOPTS_VALUE initializes the parser's byte offsets below zero while its
first frame offset is zero. FFmpeg's first-picture timestamp lookup then
fails, and GE's existing fallback stamps the buffered I-picture with the
next packet's PTS. P17 returns MPEG frame 0 at 120 ms instead of 0.

Start the parser's byte domain at zero. FFmpeg advances its internal byte
offset from consumed input; no caller-side offset state is needed. Use the
same position convention at drain. Keep PTS/DTS arguments and all fallback,
drain, queue and Flush behavior unchanged.

The P17-library native control reproduces the old first-picture defect for
seven MPEG-1/2 Matroska/PS/TS fixtures and three exact SourceReader-metadata
replays. With this argument change all ten match direct decoding at every
frame, with identical pixel hashes and counts. This is proposed P18 work,
not a built Wine/runtime pass. Require both-architecture header compilation,
H.264 parser/Flush controls, and the frozen Wine timestamp/runtime gates.
---
diff --git a/dlls/winedmo/unix_transform.c b/dlls/winedmo/unix_transform.c
--- a/dlls/winedmo/unix_transform.c
+++ b/dlls/winedmo/unix_transform.c
@@ -1157,7 +1157,7 @@ NTSTATUS transform_push_input( void *arg )
             int consumed;
 
             consumed = av_parser_parse2( t->parser, t->avctx, &parsed_data, &parsed_size,
-                                         data, size, t->packet->pts, t->packet->dts, AV_NOPTS_VALUE );
+                                         data, size, t->packet->pts, t->packet->dts, 0 );
             if (consumed < 0)
                 return STATUS_UNSUCCESSFUL;
 
@@ -1671,7 +1671,7 @@ NTSTATUS transform_drain( void *arg )
         if (t->parser)
         {
             if (av_parser_parse2( t->parser, t->avctx, &data, &size, NULL, 0,
-                                 AV_NOPTS_VALUE, AV_NOPTS_VALUE, AV_NOPTS_VALUE ) < 0)
+                                 AV_NOPTS_VALUE, AV_NOPTS_VALUE, 0 ) < 0)
                 return (t->drain_status = STATUS_UNSUCCESSFUL);
         }
         else if (t->mpeg_es_assemble && t->mpeg_es_size)
